      ":question/id": "1fcc6561-ad5c-505f-ab2b-68056704b5b9",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=6-3x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-5,-1)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-3$ and $y$-intercept $6,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/13ab0f4f50248f2f7ab68b4fe9072e35ee580a7951fadbce00705e941a1f54cb-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (-3,\\infty)$ and $x\\in (-5,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
