  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a3f6aa6-d2f2-51ed-8854-b1fb055a5c56",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=1-2x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (3,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (1,5)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-2$ and $y$-intercept $1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/2ae4b7372caf4492fa3d7e63a069bce626023a2c5b0c520b6fe2ffd855daf0f4-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (3,\\infty)$ and $x\\in (1,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
