    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0528d944-c0e4-5d64-8e37-4134e21f446b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=2x+2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (8,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [-7,3)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $2$ and $y$-intercept $2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/3d636f53f7e511f05c70e8aab274d7a4c54b313526c1eca26edcaae71d8b315f-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (8,\\infty)$ and $x\\in [-7,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
